codemap 8
path cli-wire
kind layer
author ai
group cli
note wire.rs: everything in the cli crate that is text. Inbound, the clap types: the Command enum, one variant per command feature named and described from the registry, and an argument struct per command holding plain strings and numbers (convert.rs makes them domain values). Outbound, every line a command prints and every error message: exec.rs never formats, it calls a wire function with values, and Failure, MapError, io-map's load, parse and save errors and repin's LeftStale are all worded here. So changing a message is a change to this file alone. Output is grep-shaped: one item per line, file:line or file:start-end with 1-based lines, names that paste back into another command.

